Step 1: create a config yaml file
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: app-config
data:
  APP_ENV: production
  APP_DEBUG: "false"
  LOG_LEVEL: info


step 2: apply the configmap with this command
kubectl apply -f "filename"
    And verfiy 
kubectl get configmaps

NAME               DATA   AGE
app-config         3      16s
kube-root-ca.crt   1      49m

kubectl describe configmap app-config(get detailed about configmap)
Name:         app-config
Namespace:    default
Labels:       <none>
Annotations:  <none>

Data
====
APP_DEBUG:
----
false
APP_ENV:
----
production
LOG_LEVEL:
----
info
Events:  <none>


Step 3: create a configmap pod yaml file and create the pod
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: configmap-env-pod
spec:
  containers:
  - name: app
    image: nginx
    env:
    - name: APP_ENV
      valueFrom:
        configMapKeyRef:
          name: app-config
          key: APP_ENV
    - name: APP_DEBUG
      valueFrom:
        configMapKeyRef:
          name: app-config
          key: APP_DEBUG
  restartPolicy: Never


Step 4: Navigate the inside pod with this command and verify the env
kubectl exec -it configmap-env-pod -- sh
===> with the help of echo command
echo $APP_ENV
production
# echo $APP_DEBUG
false

